commit 0ba986abf35fd94fb6d9639f4a0c651405a07949
Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 09:09:29 2026 -0400

    feat(#12443): activity-heartbeat hooks (compose + poster + cycle_post)
    
    Slice (b) of #12271, agent/emitter side. Wires the heartbeat emitters
    that feed the harness /hooks/activity endpoint.
    
    - activity_hook.py (new): cross-platform heartbeat poster. As a
      PostToolUse/PostToolUseFailure async COMMAND hook it reads role from
      $SQUIDSQUAD_ROLE + payload from stdin and POSTs to the harness; also
      importable (post_activity) for cycle_post. Fail-open, always exit 0.
    - compose.py: deploys the two activity hooks into .claude/settings.json.
      These are type:command + async:true (NOT native http) — verified via the
      CC hook API that http hooks block synchronously and only command hooks
      support async, so per-tool-call hooks must be async command hooks to
      satisfy AC2 (never block/delay the tool call). Exec form (python + args
      with ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}) = cross-platform, no shell quoting. Refactored
      slice-a's _ensure_session_end_hook into a shared idempotent
      _ensure_hook_entries; added _ensure_activity_hooks.
    - cycle_post.py: _do_activity_heartbeat emits a heartbeat at cycle end
      (covers quiet stretches with no tool calls), reusing the liveness-aware
      port discovery. Fail-open.
    - installer-files.txt += activity_hook.py.
    - Tests: TestEnsureActivityHooks12443 (compose), test_activity_hook.py
      (poster fail-open + happy path), TestActivityHeartbeat12443 (cycle_post).
      Hardened test_cycle_post's #12282 egress guard to also neutralize the
      activity poster (it has its own urllib → would leak to live harness).
    
    §16 doc note (flagged to PM on the issue): 'native http, no shell wrapper'
    holds for low-frequency/teardown hooks; high-frequency telemetry hooks must
    be async command hooks. AC1 grants 'endpoint shape is skill's call'.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

